By \cref{lem:silver_reduction_sigmaap}, each queried value
$F_S(x_j)$ depends only on $S\cap 2^{M_j}$ for some finite $M_j$. Hence the entire base-level map becomes locally constant on cylinders in $\Tree_2$, and therefore Borel measurable. Consequently, the restricted height-$k$ tower is a \textit{Borel tower}
on $\Tree_2$.
